section: codegen
synopsis: x86-64 NCG: never emit an address displacement that does not fit in 32 bits
issues: #28105
mrs: !17002
description: {
  Three address forms in the x86-64 native code generator put a constant into
  the displacement of an address without checking that it fits in a signed
  32-bit integer, so the assembler rejected the module. The constant is now
  computed in a register when it does not fit.
}
